contentText:
HYBE has appointed Melissa Victor-Burkhardt as executive vp of global artist services for HYBE Global Label Services. Within the newly created role, Victor-Burkhardt will work with the company&#8217;s worldwide teams to help with project management. She will also oversee a team of project managers for marketing, commerce, distribution, DSP and streaming.

Victor-Burkhardt previously served as senior vp, head of publicity and brand strategy at Epic Records, where she worked with clients including Future, Travis Scott, 21 Savage, Giveon, Mariah The Scientist, Madison Beer and Zara Larsson. She has also worked at labels including Interscope, J Records/Jive Records, Virgin, Island Def Jam and Bad Boy Records.

&#8220;Melissa is a deeply experienced executive in the music industry who has worked across countless campaigns for global artists and has an acute understanding of the scope and teamwork required across both internal and external partners for demonstrated success,&#8221; Juan S. Arenas , president for HGLS, said in a statement. &#8220;She will work closely with our worldwide teams to strengthen and build an ecosystem that encourages services to HYBE IP, a continued collaborative approach, and a focus on high impact. I&#8217;m grateful to have her on board to help execute the vision of a globally built platform powered by best-in-class services.&#8221;

Victor-Burkhardt added, &#8220;By helping artists grow from a first single to the global stage, my work has always been about strategically building careers that last. HYBE is redefining what a music company can be, and I&#8217;m excited to bring that experience to a global platform. Thank you to Isaac Lee [CEO, HYBE Americas] and Juan S. Arenas for this opportunity.&#8221;

